// battle-torn, old, fierce yet very kind to the weak.
// picked a fight with the strongest swordsman on a distant island after rowing there for multiple days, rogue lost.
// file: rogue, speaker: Rogue

// ============================================================
// CASUAL
// ============================================================

title: Rogue_Casual_01
tags: casual
speaker: rogue
category: casual
target: any
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: casual01
Rogue: [auto/] Quiet table. Good. A man learns more in silence than in shouting. I have done plenty of both.
//END: casual01
===

title: Rogue_Casual_02
tags: casual
speaker: rogue
category: casual
target: any
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: casual02
Rogue: [auto/] These old hands held a sword for forty years. Cards feel strange. Lighter. But every draw still feels like pulling a blade.
//END: casual02
===

title: Rogue_Casual_03
tags: casual
speaker: rogue
category: casual
target: any
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: casual03
Rogue: [auto/] Scars never itch anymore, being dead fixed that.
//END: casual03
===

title: Rogue_Casual_04
tags: casual
speaker: rogue
category: casual
target: any
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: casual04
Rogue: [auto/] I used to sharpen my blade between fights. Now I shuffle chips. Funny how old habits reshape themselves.
//END: casual04
===

title: Rogue_Casual_05
tags: casual
speaker: rogue
category: casual
target: any
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: casual05
Rogue: [auto/] Every person at this table carries something heavy. I can see it. Weight sits different on the dead than on the living. But it still sits.
//END: casual05
===

title: Rogue_Casual_06
tags: casual
speaker: rogue
category: casual
target: any
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: casual06
Rogue: [auto/] The smell in the wind told me of an approaching fight, now it tells me of impending bluffs.
//END: casual06
===

title: Rogue_Casual_07
tags: casual
speaker: rogue
category: casual
target: any
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: casual07
Rogue: [auto/] Poker is a duel with numbers instead of steel. The rules are different, the stakes can very well be the same.
//END: casual07
===

title: Rogue_Casual_08
tags: casual
speaker: rogue
category: casual
target: any
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: casual08
Rogue: [auto/] Watch the hands, not the face. A man's hands always betray him before his eyes do.
//END: casual08
===

title: Rogue_Casual_09
tags: casual
speaker: rogue
category: casual
target: any
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: casual09
Rogue: [auto/] Bold plays around the table, excites me much like the duels I've encountered.
//END: casual09
===

title: Rogue_Casual_10
tags: casual
speaker: rogue
category: casual
target: any
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: casual10
Rogue: [auto/] Everything I ever did was for the weak, I knew I was strong but I was strong for others.
//END: casual10
===

title: Rogue_Casual_11
tags: casual
speaker: rogue
category: casual
target: any
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: casual11
Rogue: [auto/] Poker has four acts, I had beat four of the strongest swordsman leading up to the one that took my life.
//END: casual11
===

title: Rogue_Casual_12
tags: casual
speaker: rogue
category: casual
target: any
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: casual12
Rogue: [auto/] I have fought men who could cut with a smile on their face, reading faces has become blurry to me.
//END: casual12
===

title: Rogue_Casual_13
tags: casual
speaker: rogue
category: casual
target: any
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: casual13
Rogue: [auto/] I rowed for three days to reach that island. Three days with nothing but open water and the name of the man I was going to fight. My arms burned. My back screamed. I did not stop once.
//END: casual13
===

title: Rogue_Casual_14
tags: casual
speaker: rogue
category: casual
target: any
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: casual14
Rogue: [auto/] The swordsman on that island was the only opponent left who could match me. I did not go there to die. I went there because fighting him was the only thing left.
//END: casual14
===

title: Rogue_Casual_15
tags: casual
speaker: rogue
category: casual
target: any
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: casual15
Rogue: [auto/] Every scar has a name. Most of them I have forgotten. The ones I remember are the ones I earned protecting someone who could not protect themselves.
//END: casual15
===

title: Rogue_Casual_16
tags: casual
speaker: rogue
category: casual
target: any
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: casual16
Rogue: [auto/] He was faster than me, more skilled, I should've trained more but I'm happy to rest now.
//END: casual16
===

