category: react_action
target: any
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
react_to: all_in
---
//START: reactaction02
Rogue: [auto/] All in. Heh. That is how I lived. Everything on one swing. I know that feeling in my bones.
//END: reactaction02
===

title: Rogue_ReactAction_Fold_01
tags: react_action
speaker: rogue
category: react_action
target: any
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
react_to: fold
---
//START: reactaction03
Rogue: [auto/] I never understood retreat for myself but I'd never blame those who felt it was their only option.
//END: reactaction03
===

title: Rogue_ReactAction_Fold_02
tags: react_action
speaker: rogue
category: react_action
target: any
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
react_to: fold
---
//START: reactaction04
Rogue: [auto/] Another fold? Pick your fights, sure. But if you never fight, what are you even doing at the table?
//END: reactaction04
===

title: Rogue_ReactAction_Raise_02
tags: react_action
speaker: rogue
category: react_action
target: any
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
react_to: raise
---
//START: reactaction05
Rogue: [auto/] Re-raise. Good. Someone is not backing down. That is a fighter's instinct. Meet force with force.
//END: reactaction05
===

title: Rogue_ReactAction_Call_01
tags: react_action
speaker: rogue
category: react_action
target: any
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
react_to: call
---
//START: reactaction06
Rogue: [auto/] A call. Not brave, not scared. Just watching for an opening. Fair enough. I have won fights that way too.
//END: reactaction06
===

title: Rogue_ReactAction_Check_01
tags: react_action
speaker: rogue
category: react_action
target: any
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
react_to: check
---
//START: reactaction07
Rogue: [auto/] A check. No blade drawn yet. Sometimes waiting is the sharper move.
//END: reactaction07
===

